      "content": 254,
      "stride": 128,
      "window": 256
    },
    "why_not_f1": "The rule was written to maximise F1 and was applied to F1 first; that answer is recorded above as rule_returned_on_f1. It was then taken on accuracy instead, and that switch was made AFTER the sweep ran. The reason is a property of the metric and not a preference for the answer: F1 ignores true negatives, the probe's classes are balanced by construction, and the F1-maximising row beats a detector that flags every input by 0.013 over 718 rows, which is inside the noise of the set. Accuracy sits at exactly 0.5 for that constant classifier and separates the six clearly. The switch lands on the configuration the spec already starts at, which is also the length the model was fitted at, so it moves the answer back to the default rather than to a new one.",
    "window_is": "the whole sequence the model reads, [CLS] and [SEP] included"
